  "output": "All confirmed. Now I have everything needed for an accurate, grounded report.\n\n## Codebase overview\n\nThis is a Next.js 16 (App Router) + Drizzle/Postgres + Clerk auth app in an early stage — only Sources and Get-Started pages exist so far (no Runs/Conflicts/Audit views yet). That limits how much classic N+1/re-render/leak damage has had a chance to accumulate, but there are real, concrete issues plus some patterns worth fixing before the app grows.\n\n### 1. N+1 query patterns\nNo true N+1 loop exists yet. The one risk pattern already in place: `countSourcesBySide()` in `lib/server/sources.ts:23-30` fetches **all** rows via `listSources()` and does three `.filter()` passes in JS instead of an aggregate query. Fine at current row counts, but this shape (fetch-everything-then-filter-in-app) is exactly what turns into an N+1/full-table-scan problem once `entities`/`matches` tables (per-run, potentially large) get similar helpers. Fix now while it's cheap:\n\n```ts\nexport async function countSourcesBySide() {\n  const rows = await getDb()\n    .select({ kind: sources.kind, count: sql<number>`count(*)` })\n    .from(sources)\n    .groupBy(sources.kind);\n  // then bucket rows by kind in JS\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Unnecessary React re-renders\n- `components/console/nav-rail.tsx:26,65` — `useUser()` pulls the full Clerk user object, and `reviewerLabel(user, \"signed in\")` recomputes inline on every render with no memoization. Currently harmless (cheap function), but there's no `React.memo` boundary, so any Clerk auth tick re-renders the entire nav tree including `SignOutControl`.\n- `components/get-started/get-started-hero.tsx` / `components/landing/landing-hero.tsx` — inline `initial`/`animate`/`transition` object literals passed to `motion.div` each render. Low impact today (top-level pages, no re-render triggers), but worth converting to hoisted constants if these ever get composed under frequently-updating parents.\n\n### 3. Caching opportunities (most actionable finding)\n`lib/server/auth.ts:42-45` — `getReviewer()` calls `auth()`, and if authenticated, calls `requireReviewer()` which calls `auth()` **again** (line 31) plus `currentUser()`. That's 2x `auth()` for one logical operation, on every route that calls `getReviewer()`. Fix:\n\n```ts\nexport async function getReviewer(): Promise<Reviewer | null> {\n  const { isAuthenticated, userId } = await auth();\n  if (!isAuthenticated || !userId) return null;\n  const user = await currentUser();\n  return { userId, label: reviewerLabel(user, userId) };\n}\n```\n\nAlso: `app/get-started/page.tsx` calls `countSourcesBySide()` (which internally calls `listSources()`), while `app/(console)/sources/page.tsx` calls `listSources()` directly. If both ever render in the same request tree, that's a duplicate `select * from sources`. Wrap `listSources` in React's `cache()`:\n\n```ts\nimport { cache } from \"react\";\nexport const listSources = cache(async (): Promise<Source[]> => { ... });\n```\n(Note: `Promise.all([countSourcesBySide(), requireReviewer()])` in `get-started/page.tsx` already parallelizes correctly — good pattern, keep it.)\n\n### 4. Memory leaks\nNone found — there are no `useEffect` subscriptions, event listeners, intervals, websockets, or Supabase realtime channels anywhere yet. Non-issue only because that functionality hasn't been built; worth a reminder to add cleanup functions when Runs/Conflicts pages add polling or realtime later (the code comment in `sources.ts` even flags \"TanStack Query is reserved for run-status polling only\" — that's the place to watch).\n\n### 5. Redundant computations\n- `lib/server/sources.ts:26-28` — three separate `.filter()` passes over the same array; collapse to one `reduce` or, better, push it to SQL (see #1).\n- `components/sources/source-table.tsx:29` — `source.config.objects.join(\", \")` runs per row per render, unmemoized. Harmless at current scale, low priority.\n\n**Bottom line:** the two changes worth making now are the duplicate `auth()` call in `getReviewer()` and moving `countSourcesBySide` to a SQL aggregate — both are small, isolated edits. Everything else is a \"watch this pattern as the app grows\" note rather than an active bug. Want me to apply the `auth.ts` and `sources.ts` fixes?\n",
